@h1 Choose your path h1@

You've seen the shape of Wit — prose by default, structure when you reach for
it. Where you go next depends on what you're here to do.

@h2 ✍ I want to write h2@

Keep a manuscript in git as plain text and compile reader-ready drafts in
seconds. You'll learn prose, headings, lists, and quotes; then reusable
components, citations, and multi-file manuscripts; then the draft-in-git
workflow that ties it together.

@ul
@li Start with the writing basics and build up to a full manuscript. li@
ul@

@h2 ⌨ I want to build h2@

Use @@@code @witlang/parser code@@@ in your own app, walk the typed AST, load
external data, or write a custom renderer. You'll learn the pipeline, the AST,
the embedding API, and the @code DataLoader code@ seam.

@ul
@li Start with the architecture and the API. li@
ul@

@h2 Just looking something up? h2@

The @a |href ../../reference/core-vocabulary/| reference a@ has every node,
flag, and error. The playground lets you edit Wit and see the result live in the
browser.
